language variant
language en-earth
name overlord
gender male 60

// OVERLORD — ancient AND leader, in one voice.
//
// This is not a third voice that resembles two others. Every number below is
// taken from `ancient` or from `leaderofearth`, and where they disagree the
// file says which one won and why. The two disagree about exactly one thing,
// and it is the interesting thing: LEADER moves to persuade, ANCIENT refuses
// to move at all. OVERLORD does not split the difference — it takes ancient's
// refusal and leader's mass, because the top of a hierarchy does not persuade.
//
// The layering (overlay + octave) is NOT in this file. espeak renders one
// voice per pass; depth is built in render_overlord.py, which mixes several
// passes of THIS variant. See that file for the measured intervals.

// LOWER THAN EITHER PARENT, AND FLATTER THAN BOTH.
// leader is 70/142 (base/range) and measures f0 117.3 Hz; ancient is 98/98 —
// a range of ZERO, which is the whole of ancient's argument. OVERLORD goes
// below both and keeps ancient's refusal to modulate.
//
// MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. espeak's `pitch` maps linearly to f0 at ~0.97x over
// 40-98 (swept: 40->40.1, 50->47.2, 58->55.3, 70->67.0, 82->79.0, 98->95.0).
// So 82 is 79.0 Hz: a fifth below leader, a tone and a half below ancient, and
// still a speaking voice. An earlier draft sat at 58 -> 55.3 Hz, which is under
// the bottom of the male range and turns to buzz on any small speaker. The
// weight that draft was reaching for is not the body's job — it is the OCTAVE
// layer's, and that layer is built in render_overlord.py at exactly half of
// whatever this line says. Depth comes from underneath the voice, not from
// dragging the voice down into the mud with it.
//
// The range is 10 units, not zero, only because a perfectly dead line reads as
// a synthesiser rather than as a decision.
pitch 82 92

// LEADER'S CURVE, ANCIENT'S BOTTOM.
// leader:  165 255 / 300 205 / 700 130 / 1400 150 / 3000 180  (presence 23.7%)
// ancient: 180 190 / 380 150 / 1300 195 / 2900 140
// The scoop at 700 Hz is leader's and it is why leader is heavy without being
// muddy — it is kept exactly. The 3 kHz lift is also leader's and it is the
// clarity; it is raised further (180 -> 195) because this voice sits an octave
// lower and needs more help from the presence band, not less. The bottom
// anchor at 165 is pushed to full 260 because the fundamental is now at 58.
tone 165 260 300 210 700 128 1400 155 3000 195

// Chest from leader, thinning from ancient.
// F0-F2 are leader's (mass); F3-F5 sit between the two parents; F6-F8 take
// ancient's steeper fall, which is what age does to the top of a voice. The
// result has leader's body and ancient's decay.
formant 0 102 134 150
formant 1 100 128 144
formant 2 102 114 124
formant 3  98 106 102
formant 4  92  99  84
formant 5  86  88  60
formant 6  76  80  38
formant 7  70  76  24
formant 8  66  72  18

// THE TEXTURE IS ANCIENT'S, THE STEADINESS IS LEADER'S.
// ancient has roughness 5 and flutter 3: rasp and the tremor of age. leader has
// roughness 2 and flutter 0: no waver, ever. OVERLORD takes roughness 3 — the
// rasp survives as grain but stops being a wobble — and leader's flutter 0,
// because a tremor is a body failing and this voice is not failing.
// voicing takes leader's 96 (full fold closure, real tone) over ancient's 54
// (a whisper with something behind it): at 58 Hz there is no room for breath.
flutter 0
roughness 3
voicing 96
breath 0 1 1 1 1 1 1 0
breathw 60 70 80 80 80 80 70 60

// Consonants are pushed above BOTH parents (leader 92 80, ancient 92 84).
// A voice this low loses the top of every stop and fricative; the enunciation
// en-earth was built for has to be paid for again down here.
consonants 96 88

// ancient 80/12, leader 165/20. OVERLORD takes leader's room and lengthens it:
// the biggest space in the set, because it is the last voice you hear.
echo 180 22

// ANCIENT WINS THE ARGUMENT.
// leader still lifts its top two stress levels (+55, +80 cents) — it drives.
// ancient lifts NOTHING: stressAdd is zero at every level, and emphasis exists
// only as amplitude. That is the difference between commanding and deciding,
// and OVERLORD decides. So stressAdd is ancient's (all zero) and stressAmp is
// leader's curve carried further (29/32 -> 33/38): nothing is ever raised in
// pitch to make a point, and what does the pointing is weight.
intonation 3
stressAmp   16 16 18 21 24 28 33 38
stressAdd    0  0  0  0  0  0  0  0
